    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "When $P(x)=ax^4+x^3+bx^2+x+1$ is divided by $x-2$, the remainder is $15$, and when divided by $x+1$, the remainder is $3$. Find $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-1,\\ b=5$",
      "worked": "By the remainder theorem, $P(2)=15$ and $P(-1)=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(2)&=16a+8+4b+2+1\\\\16a+4b+11&=15\\\\4a+b&=1\\qquad(1)\\\\P(-1)&=a-1+b-1+1\\\\a+b-1&=3\\\\a+b&=4\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (2) from (1).\n$$\\begin{align*}3a&=-3\\\\a&=-1\\\\b&=4-(-1)\\\\b&=5\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
